        "worked_solution": "Note that plugging in $x=2$ gives the indeterminate form $\\frac{0}{0}.$ However, we can use L'Hopital's rule to find this limit:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to 2}\\frac{5{x}^{2}-3x-14}{{x}^{2}+x-6} & ={lim}_{x\\to 2}\\frac{[5{x}^{2}-3x-14]^{\u2032}}{[{x}^{2}+x-6]^{\u2032}} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to 2}\\frac{10x-3}{2x+1} \\\\  & =\\frac{10(2)-3}{2(2)+1} \\\\  & =\\frac{17}{5}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
